# Repo-side record of unit contents as last installed on the VPS (read by
# cloud/tests/test_unit_install_acknowledgment.py).
#
# Format: `<sha256>  <unit-name>` (two spaces). A commit that edits a unit in
# cloud/services/ must either bump its entry here in the same commit as the
# root install-copy (install -m 0644 cloud/services/<unit> /etc/systemd/system/
# && systemctl daemon-reload), or add a drift-allowlist acknowledgment
# (unit-mismatch:<name> / not-installed:<name>) for the pending-install window.
# Units acknowledged in config/drift-allowlist.conf are deliberately absent,
# EXCEPT where an entry is explicitly marked "pending root install-copy" below:
# that hash is pre-recorded at the content the operator is expected to install,
# so the acknowledgment can be dropped in the same commit as the install with
# no second manifest bump owed. A pre-recorded entry is not proof of install --
# the drift-allowlist acknowledgment is what says the host does not have it yet.
#
# Regenerate an entry: shasum -a 256 cloud/services/<unit-name>
